    "review_notes": "The upstream export predates fractional indices: none of its 32 elements has an `index`, which the pinned reference oracle requires and Excalidraw's restore assigns in array order. The retained scene inserts exactly `\"index\":\"<key>\",` after each element's opening brace, with the keys fractional-indexing 3.2.0 generateNKeysBetween(null, null, 32) produces (a0..aV); every other byte, including number spelling, is the upstream file. Content review otherwise unchanged: the eight text elements are short conversational chat lines; the two embedded image/svg+xml payloads are cartoon avatars with no marks (tests/public-scenes/README.md). Frame names are 'Slide N' labels, including the upstream typo 'Sldie 4', kept verbatim. Promotion sign-off remains pending.",
